# Put the interfaces in their zones (this changes traffic at once):
# Written inactive:
#   sl-edge-20-replies: every service but some: a service object of ZLD lists what it matches
#   sl-edge-12: not converted: TCP flags: the rule matches some packets of a connection and not others
#   ThreatSignaturesMalwareStrictOrder-1: not converted: rule group ThreatSignaturesMalwareStrictOrder is not in the input; add the answer of describe-rule-group for arn:aws:network-firewall:eu-west-1:aws-managed:stateful-rulegroup/ThreatSignaturesMalwareStrictOrder (an AWS managed rule group, whose rul
#   sf-app-1005: references 'branches': the entries of prefix list pl-0f9e8d7c6b5a40321 are not in the input (add the answer of aws ec2 get-managed-prefix-list-entries, wrapped with its PrefixListId)
#   sf-app-1005-rev: references 'branches': the entries of prefix list pl-0f9e8d7c6b5a40321 are not in the input (add the answer of aws ec2 get-managed-prefix-list-entries, wrapped with its PrefixListId)
#   stateful-default-not-tcp: every service but some: a service object of ZLD lists what it matches
#   sf-app-1006: not converted: keyword http.uri; not converted: keyword content: /admin
#   dl-block-1: not converted: tls.sni: the rule matches by domain name, which is not an address
#   dl-egress-1: not converted: tls.sni: the rule matches by domain name, which is not an address
#   dl-egress-3: not converted: http.host: the rule matches by domain name, which is not an address
